   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5543aaec-8dc0-4800-933d-1c3e91e0161a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Predicting White Wine Quality Using Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This project uses machine learning to predict the quality score of white wine based on its physicochemical properties. The analysis examines characteristics such as acidity, sugar content, density, pH, sulphates, and alcohol.\n",
    "\n",
    "The project follows a regression approach because the target variable, `quality`, is a numerical score.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective is to investigate whether physicochemical measurements can be used to predict white wine quality. Such a model could support quality-control processes in the wine and beverage industry by providing an initial data-driven quality assessment."
   ]
  },
